    {
      "slug": "noah-s-ark-poulakis",
      "title": "Noah's Ark (Poulakis)",
      "year": 1635,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a1/Noah%27s_Ark_by_T.Poulakis_after_engraving_of_J.Sadeler_%2817th_c.%29.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 3493,
      "imageHeight": 2700,
      "story": "Noah's Ark is a tempera painting by Theodore Poulakis. Poulakis was a Greek Baroque painter and teacher. He was a member of both the Late Cretan School and the Heptanese School. He is often regarded as the father of the Heptanese School. He was active from 1635 to 1692. By the age of 24, he was living in Venice. He stayed in the city for thirteen years. He was involved in local politics. He frequently traveled all over the Ionian Islands and settled in Corfu. He also regularly returned to Venice. Over 130 of his paintings have survived and can be found all over the world.",
      "facts": [
        "The works of de Vos and Sadeler share common characteristics with Poulaki's work.",
        "Poulaki's painting more closely resembles Sadeler's engraving."
      ],
      "wikipediaUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noah's_Ark_(Poulakis)",
